  "body": "## What was broken\n\nEvery admin save rewrote `~/.fcc/.env` with **54 empty `FCC_SMOKE_*` keys** under a `# Smoke Tests` header — 13% of a 414-line file.\n\nMeasured by executing the writer, not by reading it:\n\n```\ntotal KEY=VALUE lines written : 414\nFCC_SMOKE_* lines written     :  54\nshare of file that is smoke   : 13.0%\n```\n\nConfirmed present in a real user's live 420-line `.env`, header at line 366.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe manifest registered a `smoke` section with 54 `ConfigFieldSpec` entries, and `render_env_file` iterates **all** `FIELDS` unconditionally. No view in `admin.js` claims that section (`grep -i smoke admin.js` → **0 hits**), so the fields rendered nowhere while still being written to disk on every save. Nothing in `src/` reads them either — only `smoke/` tooling does, straight from `os.environ`.\n\n## Why this is two changes, not one\n\nRetiring them from the manifest **alone would have made things worse**.\n\n`unmanaged_env_values()` preserves an unmanaged key only when `key in settings_env_aliases()`. These are not Settings fields — that is the whole finding. So a user who had actually set `FCC_SMOKE_MODEL_OPENAI=gpt-4o-mini` to run smoke tests would have had that value **silently deleted** on their next save. Same \"a form must not delete what it cannot see\" bug class this project already fixed once.\n\nSo:\n\n1. **Remove** the `smoke` section and its 54 fields from the admin manifest. The smoke tooling is untouched and keeps reading `os.environ`.\n2. **Widen** `unmanaged_env_values()`: also preserve keys under the project's own `FCC_` prefix when they hold a **non-empty** value, even though no Settings alias reads them. Empty values still drop, so existing files self-clean. Non-`FCC_` keys keep the strict rule, so genuinely retired options still retire.\n\nThe now-dead `\"smoke\"` entry in `KNOWN_UNRENDERED` is removed too — leaving it would keep a permanent blind spot in the guard that exists to catch exactly this.\n\n`.env.example` **keeps** its smoke block deliberately: those are still real, settable env vars, just no longer admin-managed.\n\n## Verification\n\nRound-tripped a **sanitised copy of a real 441-line user `.env`** (all credential values redacted before reading; original untouched) through the actual load→save path, with a populated smoke key added to simulate a real user:\n\n```\nlines before            : 415\nlines after             : 361\nFCC_SMOKE before        : 55\nFCC_SMOKE after         : 1  -> ['FCC_SMOKE_MODEL_OPENAI=gpt-4o-mini']\n\"# Smoke Tests\" header  : False\n\n  PASS  populated smoke key survived\n  PASS  empty smoke keys gone\n  PASS  no Smoke Tests header\n  PASS  ordinary setting kept\n  PASS  no secret leaked into output\n```\n\n**Mutation-tested.** Removing the `FCC_` preserve branch reproduces the exact data loss this PR exists to prevent:\n\n```\nFCC_SMOKE after         : 0  -> []\n  FAIL  populated smoke key survived\n  FAIL  empty smoke keys gone\n```\n\nRe-adding a single smoke field to the manifest fails the no-smoke-keys tests by name.\n\n```\n6 new tests + targeted selection   101 passed\nfull suite                         4423 passed, 14 pre-existing baseline\nruff format --check                925 files already formatted\nruff check / ty check              All checks passed!\n```\n\nThe 14 baseline failures are 6 PowerShell installer tests and 8 ambient `EXA_API_KEY`/`SEARXNG` websearch tests — the documented local baseline. None touch manifest, admin, persistence or smoke.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n**Existing files self-clean on the next save, not on upgrade.** Users keep their 54 empty lines until they next press Apply in the dashboard. That is deliberate — rewriting someone's `.env` on upgrade is a bigger and riskier action than this fix warrants.\n\nThe widened preserve rule is scoped to the `FCC_` prefix, so it cannot resurrect unrelated third-party env vars. A populated `FCC_` key that is genuinely retired in future will now survive where it previously would have been dropped — an accepted trade for not destroying user configuration.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
