    "message": "fix(admin): stop writing 54 dev-only smoke keys into the user's .env\n\nEvery admin save rewrote ~/.fcc/.env with 54 empty FCC_SMOKE_* keys under\na \"# Smoke Tests\" header -- 13% of a 414-line file. Measured by executing\nrender_env_file({}, preserved={}), and confirmed present in a real user's\nlive 420-line .env.\n\nMechanism: the manifest registered a \"smoke\" section with 54\nConfigFieldSpec entries, and render_env_file iterates all FIELDS\nunconditionally. No view in admin.js claims that section (grep -i smoke\nadmin.js -> 0 hits), so the fields rendered nowhere while still being\nwritten to disk on every save. Nothing in src/ reads them either; only\nsmoke/ tooling does, straight from os.environ.\n\nRetiring them from the manifest alone would have made things worse.\nunmanaged_env_values() preserves an unmanaged key only when it is in\nsettings_env_aliases(), and these are not Settings fields -- so a user\nwho had actually set FCC_SMOKE_MODEL_OPENAI would have had that value\nsilently deleted on their next save. That is the same \"a form must not\ndelete what it cannot see\" bug this project already fixed once.\n\nSo this is two changes:\n\n1. Remove the \"smoke\" section and its 54 fields from the admin manifest.\n   The smoke tooling is untouched and keeps reading os.environ.\n2. Widen unmanaged_env_values(): also preserve keys under the project's\n   own FCC_ prefix when they hold a non-empty value, even though no\n   Settings alias reads them. Empty values still drop, so existing files\n   self-clean. Non-FCC_ keys keep the strict rule, so genuinely retired\n   options still retire.\n\nThe now-dead \"smoke\" entry in the KNOWN_UNRENDERED allow-list is removed\ntoo; leaving it would keep a permanent blind spot in the guard that is\nsupposed to catch exactly this bug class.\n\n.env.example keeps its smoke block deliberately: those are still real,\nsettable env vars, just no longer admin-managed.\n\nVerification:\n- 6 new tests, including a round-trip proving a populated smoke key\n  survives a save byte-exact while empty ones vanish.\n- Round-tripped a sanitised copy of a real 441-line user .env through the\n  load/save path: 415 -> 361 KEY=VALUE lines, FCC_SMOKE 55 -> 1, the\n  populated key preserved, ordinary settings unchanged, no secret in the\n  output.\n- Mutation-tested: removing the FCC_ preserve branch destroys the\n  populated smoke value and fails the round-trip tests by name;\n  re-adding one smoke field fails the no-smoke-keys tests by name.\n- Full suite: 4423 passed, 14 pre-existing baseline failures (6\n  PowerShell installer, 8 ambient EXA_API_KEY/SEARXNG), none in\n  manifest/admin/persistence/smoke.\n- ruff format --check, ruff check, ty check: all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
